    "body": "## Summary\n- allow Stripe automatic payment methods that require redirects for wallet top-ups\n- keep signed server-side webhook settlement as the only wallet credit authority\n- immediately scrub Stripe return parameters, including `payment_intent_client_secret`, from the wallet URL before async Stripe work\n- require the wallet-specific `topup=return` marker before handling Stripe return parameters\n- preserve unrelated query parameters, hash, and existing browser history state\n- add backend redirect-method regression coverage and dependency-free frontend return-flow tests\n- run frontend tests in the standard Web verify CI job\n- document wallet payment idempotency, privacy, and settlement invariants\n\n## Safety / data model\n- no Flyway migration: persisted schema and ledger semantics are unchanged\n- no browser `redirect_status` or retrieved PaymentIntent status credits the wallet\n- idempotent signed webhook settlement remains authoritative\n\n## Validation\nCI must pass on the latest PR head before merge, including API verify, Web verify, containers/runtime smoke and path-triggered payments ledger coverage.",
